INT. PET CEMETERY - GIFT SHOP - DAY

A cramped shop inside a converted barn. Shelves of tiny urns, plush angel wings, paw-print stepping stones. A cash register shaped like a bone. Soft harp music drifts from a speaker.

FENELLA ABERNATHY, 50s, in a lavender smock, arranges a display of memorial candles. She hums with the harp.

Behind the counter, TOBY QUINN, 20s, scrolls on his phone, a name tag reading TOBY (ASK ME ABOUT GRIEF).

The door jingles. A MAN IN A TRACKSUIT, 40s, sunglasses on indoors, steps in carrying a shoebox.

TRACKSUIT MAN
Hi. I'd like to bury a hamster.

FENELLA
(warmly)
Oh. I'm so sorry for your loss.

TRACKSUIT MAN
It's not a loss. It's a business decision.

Fenella tilts her head. Toby sets his phone down.

TOBY
What kind of hamster?

TRACKSUIT MAN
The kind that owes me money.

Silence. The harp plays on.

FENELLA
Plots start at three hundred dollars. For rodents, two hundred.

TRACKSUIT MAN
Does that include a marker?

FENELLA
Marker is extra.

TRACKSUIT MAN
What does it say?

TOBY
Whatever you want. "Beloved companion." "In loving memory."

TRACKSUIT MAN
Can it say "Dead"?

FENELLA
We would have to run that by Mr. Pruitt.

A phone on the wall rings. Fenella answers it.

FENELLA (CONT'D)
(into phone)
Rosewood Rest, this is Fenella.

PRUITT (O.S.)
(over the phone, a gravelly voice)
Fenella, it's Pruitt. Is someone trying to bury a hamster?

FENELLA
How did you know?

PRUITT (O.S.)
It's the third this week.

FENELLA
Are you quite sure it's a hamster?

PRUITT (O.S.)
I have never been sure.

Fenella covers the mouthpiece. Whispers to Toby.

FENELLA (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Mr. Pruitt says it's the third.

TOBY
(whispering)
Of what?

FENELLA
(whispering)
Of the week.

The Tracksuit Man shifts the shoebox from one arm to the other. It makes a small rattle.

TRACKSUIT MAN
Is there a problem?

TOBY
No problem, sir. Fenella, the phone.

FENELLA
(into phone)
Mr. Pruitt, I'll call you back.

She hangs up.

TRACKSUIT MAN
Do you take cash?

FENELLA
We take cash.

TOBY
We take cash.

TRACKSUIT MAN
Good. Because I'd like to pay in advance. For all of them.

He sets the shoebox on the counter. Opens the lid a crack. Fenella peeks inside. Her smile freezes. Toby leans in.

TOBY (CONT'D)
That's not a hamster.

TRACKSUIT MAN
I told you. Business decision.

FENELLA
(very calmly)
Toby. Lock the door.

Toby locks the door. The harp plays on.

TRACKSUIT MAN
(removing his sunglasses)
Now. Tell me about your grief counseling.

Fenella and Toby exchange a long look.

PRUITT (O.S.)
(through the wall speaker, faint)
Is everything all right in there?

FENELLA
(brightly, to the speaker)
Perfectly fine, Mr. Pruitt!

TOBY
(to the Tracksuit Man)
Sir, would you like a candle?

The man picks one up. Smells it.

TRACKSUIT MAN
Does this one come in lavender?

FENELLA
It comes in lavender.

TRACKSUIT MAN
Then I'll take it.

He sets down a wad of bills. Fenella counts them with trembling fingers. Toby stares at the box. The harp swells.

Slowly, Fenella slides the box off the counter and into a drawer, and shuts it as if closing a secret.
